# Device flow for one issue (ADR-0049). Copy to slices/KIT-<n>.yaml in the same PR as the slice.
#
# Cover only what THIS issue changes: one step per Acceptance criterion that is
# visible on a screen, and nothing else. Do not re-walk the whole app.
#
# design-sections: Sheet, Button dock
#   ^ the docs/design-system.md sections the review reads for this flow, besides
#     Color, Typography, Spacing and Layout, which are always read. Names as in
#     docs/design-system.md headings. Leave the list empty if none apply.
#
# Rules
# - `name:` is the issue key in lower case, `kit-<n>`. Screenshots are named
#   kc__kit-<n>__<step>, <step> being NN-what-it-shows (lower case, digits, hyphens).
# - Tap by `testID`, never by copy. A new control a step must tap gets its testID
#   in this PR. Adding a testID is not a UI change.
# - Reach the screen through ../subflows/sign-in.yaml (signed in as the Test
#   Collector, data reset) or, for a signed-out slice, reset the data and launch
#   with clearState as sign-in.yaml does. Do not replay other issues' screens.
# - Each Acceptance criterion that a screen can show gets one takeScreenshot at
#   the moment it shows. Name the criterion in a comment above the step.
appId: app.kitcollective.mobile
name: kit-000
---
- runFlow:
    file: ../subflows/sign-in.yaml
    env:
      EMAIL: ${MAESTRO_COLLECTOR_EMAIL}
      PASSWORD: ${MAESTRO_COLLECTOR_PASSWORD}
- startRecording: kc__kit-000
# AC 1: <what the criterion says>
- tapOn:
    id: <testID of the control>
- extendedWaitUntil:
    visible:
      id: <testID of the screen the control opens>
    timeout: 15000
- waitForAnimationToEnd:
    timeout: 5000
- takeScreenshot: kc__kit-000__01-<what-it-shows>
- stopRecording
